WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:04.170
-Before we move on, we would
like to take a moment.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.039
This weekend,
five people were killed

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:08.507
and many more were injured
when a gunman opened fire

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:11.544
at an LGBTQ nightclub
in Colorado.

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.580
Our hearts go out to the victims
and their families,

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.282
and to the entire
LGBTQ community.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.184
One of our writers, Jenny Hagel,
is gay,

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.186
and she's here to comment.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.754
-Thanks, Seth.

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.857
When I read the news about
Colorado on Sunday morning,

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:27.360
I was shocked.
But also, I wasn't shocked.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.929
Because sadly, our culture
is filled with messages

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.298
that there is something wrong
with queer people.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:36.235
That we are, at best, weird
and, at worst, sick.

00:00:36.235 --> 00:00:38.972
And those messages,
whether it's something small,

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.407
like telling a little boy
he can't wear nail polish,

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:43.809
or something big,
like passing a law

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:46.312
that says queer people
can't adopt children,

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.816
they all contribute to the
dehumanization of queer people.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:52.351
And once a group of people
is seen as less than human,

00:00:52.351 --> 00:00:54.386
it's easy to hurt them.

00:00:54.386 --> 00:00:57.290
I'm sure that for many,
what happened in Colorado

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.425
will be seen as the result
of our nation's obsession

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:02.462
with guns,
and that's part of it, for sure.

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:04.663
But it's also
the result of our culture's

00:01:04.663 --> 00:01:07.867
deep-seated
homophobia and transphobia,

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.303
our unhealthy relationship
with masculinity,

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:12.705
and our nation's tendency
to allow religion

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:15.007
to be used
as a cover for prejudice.

00:01:15.007 --> 00:01:18.277
And the way our nation's history
of racism intersects with

00:01:18.277 --> 00:01:20.279
and compounds all those things.

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:24.517
Now, that's a lot to untangle,
and I don't know how to do it.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.686
So, instead,
I just wanted to say

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.221
that despite the millions
of voices in our culture

00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:31.991
saying that there is something
wrong with queer people,

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:35.194
that we're sick or deviant
or predatory

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:37.330
or just a little off,

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.833
we are totally, 100% normal.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:43.636
We live the same way
that everyone else does.

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.071
We want the same things.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:48.474
We are great in the same ways
and boring in the same ways.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:51.644
We're just regular people.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:54.280
If you're queer, I wanted to say

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.883
that I see you
and I'm grieving with you.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:59.018
And in this week
of giving thanks,

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:02.288
one thing I'm deeply,
deeply thankful for

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.623
is the LGBTQ community.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.726
And if you're queer
but you're not out,

00:02:07.726 --> 00:02:09.528
because you don't feel
ready to be

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:12.031
or because it's not safe
for you to be,

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.767
I see you, too,
and I think you are great

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.870
and perfect
just the way you are.

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.239
Nothing about us
needs to be fixed,

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:21.707
but there is
something in America

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.909
that desperately needs fixing,

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:26.345
and I hope we figure out soon
how to do it.

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:27.847
Thank you.

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:30.082
[ Applause ]
-Jenny Hagel, everyone.

00:02:30.082 --> 00:02:31.751
Thank you, Jenny.

